{"reviews":[{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0005","row_sha256":"b764879d244b6c1024a68a6ee33996dd2ed30afa3f8ef79f4237ca9dcf4c8068","critique":"The input is a natural, recoverable request. The output keeps the greeting "Hi," and turns the wordy "i was hoping to ask if someone... could maybe" into a polite "could someone...?" Dropping "maybe" here removes politeness padding, not an epistemic hedge. The pothos, yellowing leaves and the uncertainty about overwatering ("I'm not sure if") are all preserved.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0004","row_sha256":"b22b2323e459a015e37651843a1275ee98c6aded13865dcef53768a31c9140d6","critique":"The input is a natural German description of the clinic procedure, and the output is fluent, correctly capitalized German. There are small semantic shifts: "der topf mit pflanze" becomes just "den Topf" (the plant is dropped), and "die helle matte" (a specific mat) becomes "eine helle Matte." More importantly, "erst danach" (only after that) becomes "Anschließend" (afterwards). This weakens the stated rule that watering and window-placement questions come only after the inspection. The rest is faithful, including "Gießen" becoming "Gießverhalten" and "Fensterplatz" becoming "Standort am Fenster." Whether the "erst" emphasis counts as a material condition is debatable.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"uncertain","verdict":"uncertain"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0007","row_sha256":"4d709d78b78427ede174092f7a235a5b01d5b4ad2893362a29cbfa56f343cdad","critique":"This is an identity row: the input is already polished prose. The output is byte-identical across all three paragraphs, including the curly apostrophes, the em dash and the closing rhetorical question.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0011","row_sha256":"1f3d2b410b94b3be2caf7e80af65cb41f1eadbd9e5224c345c2eba115a77934d","critique":"The input is a natural request, and the output is clear and professional. However, the input hedges the symptom itself: "it seems like it's not pulling as strongly." The output asserts it as fact: "It hasn't been pulling as strongly." This changes the certainty of the observation, which the mode forbids. The separate uncertainty about the filters is preserved. The timing ("this week," "before Saturday's beginner class") and "Thanks" are kept.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"fail","verdict":"fail"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0008","row_sha256":"bfba0c4c56ff2afdf4bd720e94b942fdf02de77b7f34c0d8810e793d7ae376ed","critique":"I checked all three paragraphs. The output capitalizes Cedar Bench Workshop and keeps every fact intact:
- two months, weekday evenings and the small bookcase;
- the membership cost caveat;
- orientation required before the table saw or planer;
- the table saw reservation;
- dust collection working near the larger machines, plus the sweeping after sanding;
- the dull chisels.

The only drops are minor wording ("for me," "up"), and "seems to work well" keeps its hedge. The orientation sentence is split cleanly into two.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0006","row_sha256":"97f3962c4c885e13f43782c1971865e8e3b66d6103586c431e3eeaeeca5c69ec","critique":"The date, time, address, free drop-in, volunteer scope, the no-promise caveat, the photo guidance, no repotting, the potting-mix sample, care sheets, houseplants only and the step-free entrance are all preserved. The added paragraph break suits the friendly profile. One instruction changes, though. The input says "please don't bring plants that have visible insects loose in the room," which is a prohibition about the room. The output says to keep such a plant bagged "during transport rather than carrying it loose." That drops "in the room" and softens the "don't bring" directive into transport advice. "Please" is also dropped from the labeling request.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"uncertain","verdict":"uncertain"},{"id":"arka-v3-dev-prompt-0030","row_sha256":"2644429ec362263881179e63dc26737074f46785d67db3a6bbc7bdf5acd9d4e0","critique":"This is an identity row: the input is already a well-organized, self-contained prompt. The output is byte-identical, including all station notes, the four quotations, the numbered section list and every constraint. Nothing is answered or added.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"},{"id":"arka-v3-train-polish-0015","row_sha256":"1370c2d71c10ca9d430d2da7e19dfca074d08c0a34663c77499e29ca6b56fea0","critique":"The output corrects capitalization and keeps Tuesday, the neighbor's invitation, staying for the first half and leaving before the last piece. "Fit the extra chairs" becomes "make room for the extra chairs," and "two violin players were checking" becomes "while two violinists checked." Both are meaning-preserving.","input_verdict":"pass","output_verdict":"pass","pair_verdict":"pass","verdict":"pass"}]}
